    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jacob Wilson** standing out as the clear offensive engine. With a score of 67.97, he benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Johnson (5.29 xERA) and a park environment that adds 10% to his baseline projection. While **Gunnar Henderson** (62.18) carries a slightly lower raw output, his significant platoon advantage (+14%) against Woo keeps him locked into the core. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.37) rounds out the high-confidence tier; despite facing a tough assignment in Gray, his park-adjusted upside maintains a strong floor for a Tuesday matchup.\n\nThe benching decisions were primarily dictated by a lack of volume, as key contributors like **Kyle Tucker**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Andy Pages** are sidelined by team off-days. **Miguel Vargas** (52.64) remains the most interesting start among the fringe plays. While his baseline is modest, his score is bolstered by a 2% boost from a \"slow SP delivery\" factor, which increases his probability of swiping a bag against Weathers\u2014a critical priority given our organizational focus on scarcity in stolen bases. **Brayan Rocchio** (41.39) and **Josh Jung** (42.87) represent our most precarious starts today. **Josh Jung** in particular faces a steep challenge against the high-skill arm of Ryan, and while he is currently active, he sits right on the edge of our benching threshold; should any lineup adjustments surface before first pitch, he is the primary candidate to be swapped for fresh legs like **Nasim Nunez** or **Cole Carrigg** to maintain efficiency. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding our IL-impacted depth. With **Luis Robert Jr.** officially confirmed as out, the middle infield rotation\u2014supported by **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Jorge Polanco**\u2014must continue to over-index on plate discipline to maintain our AVG standing. No major weather risks are reported, but monitor the status of **Miguel Vargas** closely, as any shift from the #3 spot would necessitate a re-evaluation of his current daily efficiency score.",
